-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Other third-party software
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The application bundles open-source components under permissive licenses
(MIT, ISC, BSD, Apache-2.0), among them Electron, React, TipTap and
ProseMirror, CodeMirror, Lezer, xterm.js, node-pty and Lucide icons, and Rust
crates such as serde, ecow and unicode-segmentation. Their license texts ship
with each package (see node_modules/*/LICENSE and the crates' sources).
Electron's and Chromium's licenses are included in every app build
(LICENSE.electron.txt, LICENSES.chromium.html).

Claude Code is a product of Anthropic; Codex is a product of OpenAI. Typewright
only starts the command-line tools that the user has installed and is not
affiliated with either company.
